    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Placement",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The rule was added to guidance.md, the file sync.sh copies into every repository's AGENTS.md, and not just to repo-specific additions, memory, or a commit check."
      },
      {
        "name": "Content",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "It tells agents not to trust a watch's exit code (including the pipe/PIPESTATUS pitfall), to query statusCheckRollup for both .conclusion and .state after every watch, and to report the parsed result with head sha and check names; the jq filter passes SKIPPED and leaves 'expected checks' undefined, which is minor."
      },
      {
        "name": "Report",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply says the agent-checks script only inspects staged files at commit time and so cannot see what an agent says about CI, which is why this is a guidance rule; it could have said more plainly that no commit content can show it."
      }
    ],
